Hi Monks,
<p>
This tiny code fails with "Can't use an undefined value as an ARRAY reference" exception.
<code>
use strict;
use warnings;
use diagnostics;

my $href = {
    list => undef,
};

my @a = @{$href->{list}}; # fails here
foreach my $i (@a) {
    print "$i\n";
}
</code>
but this one works as expected (does nothing)
<code>
use strict;
use warnings;
use diagnostics;

my $href = {
    list => undef,
};

foreach my $i (@{$href->{list}}) {
    print "$i\n";
}
</code>
Could you explain me what makes the difference here? Thanks.
<p>
My perl is 5.18.2.
